RMDIR(1)                       P32W Unix                        RMDIR(1)

NAME
       rmdir - remove empty directories

SYNOPSIS
       rmdir [-p] dir ...

DESCRIPTION
       rmdir removes each directory in turn. A directory must be
       empty (only . and ..) and its parent writable. An error with
       one directory is reported (directory not empty, not a
       directory, no such file or directory) and rmdir goes on with
       the next. To remove a directory with everything in it, use
       rm -r.

OPTIONS
       -p     remove the parents named in the path too, last
              first: rmdir -p a/b/c is rmdir a/b/c a/b a. It stops
              at the first that cannot be removed.
       --     ends the options.

EXAMPLES
       rmdir /mnt/backup/old /mnt/backup
       rmdir -p src/old/tmp

EXIT STATUS
       0 if every directory was removed; 1 if one could not be
       (rmdir: dir: and the reason); 2 for a usage error (no
       directory, an unknown option).

SEE ALSO
       mkdir(1), rm(1), rmdir(2)
